/*! @brief Console access object

 The console module is a core module that provides functionality similar to the console object in browsers, allowing information to be output to the console for debugging and information output.

 The most commonly used method in the console module is log(), which can print any JavaScript value to the console and automatically add a newline. In addition to the log() method, there are info(), warn(), error() methods for outputting information, warnings, and errors respectively. Their functions are basically the same as the log() method, only the styles displayed in the console are different.

 The console module also provides the dir() method, which outputs an object's properties and methods in a more readable form to the console, facilitating debugging of complex objects. Additionally, there are time() and timeEnd() methods for timing code execution in the console and outputting the time difference.

 In addition to the commonly used methods above, the console module provides some other methods such as assert(), notic(), trace(), etc., which can conveniently perform debugging and information output in different situations.

 The console module is a very practical module that can improve debugging efficiency during development and conveniently output various information.
 */
module console
{
    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const FATAL = 0;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const ALERT = 1;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const CRIT = 2;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const ERROR = 3;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const WARN = 4;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const NOTICE = 5;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const INFO = 6;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const DEBUG = 7;

    /*! @brief loglevel for output only, no newline after information output, file and syslog do not save this level information */
    const PRINT = 9;

    /*! @brief loglevel level constant */
    const NOTSET = 10;

    /*! @brief Output level, used to filter output information, default is NOTSET, output all. Information is filtered before being output to each device set by add.
     */
    static Integer loglevel;

    /*! @brief Query the number of characters per line in the terminal */
    static readonly Integer width;

    /*! @brief Query the number of lines in the terminal */
    static readonly Integer height;

    /*! @brief Add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     type is configuration, device name string:

     ```JavaScript
     console.add("console");
     ```

     syslog is only valid on posix platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add("syslog");
     ```

     event is only valid on windows platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add("event");
     ```

     @param type output device
     */
    static add(String type);

    /*! @brief Add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event, nslog and file, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     cfg can be a device configuration object:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add({
        type: "console",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]  // optional, default is all levels
     });
     ```

     syslog is only valid on posix platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add({
        type: "syslog",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     event is only valid on windows platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add({
        type: "event",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     nslog is only valid on Darwin platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add({
         type: "nslog",
         levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     file log:
     ```JavaScript
     console.add({
        type: "file",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR],
        path: "path/to/file_%s.log", // Specify the log output file, %s can be used to specify the date insertion position, if not specified, add to the end
        split: "30m", // Optional values are "day", "hour", "minute", "####k", "####m", "####g", default is "1m"
        count: 10 // option, selectable from 2 to 128, default is 128
     });
     ```

     @param cfg output configuration
     */
    static add(Object cfg);

    /*! @brief Batch add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event and file, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     ```JavaScript
     console.add(["console", {
        type: "syslog",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     }]);
     ```

     @param cfg output configuration array
     */
    static add(Array cfg);

    /*! @brief Add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     type is configuration, device name string:

     ```JavaScript
     console.use("console");
     ```

     syslog is only valid on posix platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use("syslog");
     ```

     event is only valid on windows platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use("event");
     ```

     @param type output device
     */
    static use(String type);

    /*! @brief Add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event, nslog and file, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     cfg can be a device configuration object:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use({
        type: "console",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]  // optional, default is all levels
     });
     ```

     syslog is only valid on posix platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use({
        type: "syslog",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     event is only valid on windows platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use({
        type: "event",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     nslog is only valid on Darwin platforms:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use({
         type: "nslog",
         levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     });
     ```

     file log:
     ```JavaScript
     console.use({
        type: "file",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR],
        path: "path/to/file_%s.log", // Specify the log output file, %s can be used to specify the date insertion position, if not specified, add to the end
        split: "30m", // Optional values are "day", "hour", "minute", "####k", "####m", "####g", default is "1m"
        count: 10 // option, selectable from 2 to 128, default is 128
     });
     ```

     @param cfg output configuration
     */
    static use(Object cfg);

    /*! @brief Batch add console output system, supported devices are console, syslog, event and file, up to 10 outputs can be added

     By configuring console, program output and system errors can be sent to different devices for runtime environment information collection.

     ```JavaScript
     console.use(["console", {
        type: "syslog",
        levels: [console.INFO, console.ERROR]
     }]);
     ```

     @param cfg output configuration array
     */
    static use(Array cfg);

    /*! @brief Initialize to default settings, only output information to console */
    static reset();

    /*! @brief Record normal log information, same as info

     Record general level log information. Usually used to output non-error prompt information.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static log(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record normal log information, same as info

     Record general level log information. Usually used to output non-error prompt information.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static log(...args);

    /*! @brief Record debug log information

     Record debug log information. Usually used to output debug information. Not important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static debug(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record debug log information

     Record debug log information. Usually used to output debug information. Not important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static debug(...args);

    /*! @brief Record normal log information, same as log

     Record general level log information. Usually used to output non-error prompt information.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static info(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record normal log information, same as log

     Record general level log information. Usually used to output non-error prompt information.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static info(...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output suggestive debug information. Generally important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static notice(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output suggestive debug information. Generally important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static notice(...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information, same as warning

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output warning debug information. Important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static warn(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information, same as warning

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output warning debug information. Important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static warn(...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output warning debug information. Important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static warning(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record warning log information

     Record warning log information. Usually used to output warning debug information. Important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static warning(...args);

    /*! @brief Record error log information

     Record error log information. Usually used to output error information. Very important. System error information is also recorded at this level.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static error(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record error log information

     Record error log information. Usually used to output error information. Very important. System error information is also recorded at this level.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static error(...args);

    /*! @brief Record critical error log information, same as critical

     Record critical error log information. Usually used to output critical error information. Very important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static crit(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record critical error log information, same as critical

     Record critical error log information. Usually used to output critical error information. Very important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static crit(...args);

    /*! @brief Record critical error log information

     Record critical error log information. Usually used to output critical error information. Very important.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static critical(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record critical error log information

     Record critical error log information. Usually used to output critical error information. Very important.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static critical(...args);

    /*! @brief Record alert error log information

     Record alert error log information. Usually used to output alert error information. Very important. Highest level information.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static alert(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Record alert error log information

     Record alert error log information. Usually used to output alert error information. Very important. Highest level information.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static alert(...args);

    /*! @brief Output current call stack

     Output current call stack through log.
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static trace(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Output current call stack

     Output current call stack through log.
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static trace(...args);

    /*! @brief Output object in JSON format

     Supports the following parameters:
     ```JavaScript
     {
         "colors": false, // Specify whether to color output, default is false
         "depth": 2, // Specify the maximum output depth, default is 2
         "table": false, // Specify whether to output in table form, default is false
         "encode_string": true, // Specify whether to encode strings, default is true
         "maxArrayLength": 100, // Specify the maximum number of array elements to display, set to 0 or negative to not display elements, default is 100
         "maxStringLength": 10000, // Specify the maximum length of output string, set to 0 or negative to not display string, default is 10000
         "fields": [], // Specify the fields to display, default is all
     }
     ```
     @param obj specify the object to process
     @param options specify format control options
     */
    static dir(Value obj, Object options = {});

    /*! @brief Output object in JSON format
     @param obj given object to display
     */
    static table(Value obj);

    /*! @brief Output object in JSON format
     @param obj given object to display
     @param fields given fields to display
     */
    static table(Value obj, Array fields);

    /*! @brief Output formatted text to console, output content is not recorded in log system, no automatic newline after output text, can output continuously
     @param fmt format string
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static print(String fmt, ...args);

    /*! @brief Output formatted text to console, output content is not recorded in log system, no automatic newline after output text, can output continuously
     @param args optional parameter list
     */
    static print(...args);

    /*! @brief Move console cursor to specified position
     @param row specify new cursor row coordinate
     @param column specify new cursor column coordinate
     */
    static moveTo(Integer row, Integer column);

    /*! @brief Hide console cursor */
    static hideCursor();

    /*! @brief Show console cursor */
    static showCursor();

    /*! @brief Clear console */
    static clear();

    /*! @brief Read user input from console
     @param msg prompt message
     @return return user input information
     */
    static String readLine(String msg = "") async;

    /*! @brief Read user input password from console
     @param msg prompt message
     @return return user input password
     */
    static String getpass(String msg = "") async;

    /*! @brief Start a timer

     @param label title, default is empty string.
     */
    static time(String label = "time");

    /*! @brief Output current timing value of specified timer

     @param label title, default is empty string.
     */
    static timeElapse(String label = "time");

    /*! @brief End specified timer and output final timing value

     @param label title, default is empty string.
     */
    static timeEnd(String label = "time");

    /*! @brief Assertion test, if test value is false, report error */
    static assert;
};